<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  REPOSITORY DRAFT — NOT XCODE-VERIFIED. NOT AN APPLE COMPLIANCE CLAIM.

  Prepared by SESSION 107 (2026-08-24) by static inspection of this
  repository (worktree at origin/main SHA 3d5da90) and of the exact
  plugin versions resolved in `pubspec.lock`, using each plugin's
  locally cached source under the Pub package cache. This app has never
  been built with Xcode/CocoaPods (no `ios/Podfile.lock` exists,
  confirmed absent) — Xcode's own manifest-merge step, which runs at
  archive time and can surface Required-Reason API usage this static
  read did not catch, has never run against this project. Final
  verification via an actual `flutter build ios`/Xcode archive is
  required before App Store submission. This file does not assert Apple
  compliance, App Store approval, or that this manifest is complete.

  Evidence this draft is based on:

  - NSPrivacyTracking / NSPrivacyTrackingDomains: set to false / empty.
    No advertising identifier (IDFA), fingerprinting, or cross-app/
    cross-site tracking code exists anywhere in lib/, android/, or ios/
    (repository-wide search); no ad or tracking SDK is declared in
    pubspec.yaml.
  - NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes: left empty. Full-repository audit found
    no personal data is collected or transmitted off-device by this
    app's own code — see docs/release/STORE_PRIVACY_FORM_DRAFT.md for
    the complete evidence and citations. (That document, not this
    comment, is the authoritative evidence record; this file only
    carries the declarations that follow from it.)
  - NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes: left empty at the app level, for the
    reasons below — this is the one section most likely to need
    revision after an actual Xcode build, and is NOT to be read as a
    claim that no Required-Reason API is used anywhere in the compiled
    app.

    Resolved iOS/macOS-relevant plugin versions (from pubspec.lock) were
    checked directly in the local Pub cache for their OWN bundled
    PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy manifests, which Xcode merges automatically
    with this file at archive time — they do not need to be duplicated
    here:
      * shared_preferences_foundation 2.5.6 — ships its own manifest
        declaring NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults, reason
        "1C8F.1" (access user defaults from within the app's own
        container). Covers this app's shared_preferences usage
        (docs/release/STORE_PRIVACY_FORM_DRAFT.md §5).
      * sqflite_darwin 2.4.3+1 — ships its own manifest, declares no
        Required-Reason API usage.
      * package_info_plus 10.2.0 (ios/ and macos/ variants) — ships its
        own manifest, declares no Required-Reason API usage.

    The following resolved plugins have real native Darwin
    implementations (confirmed: their `darwin/` source directories
    exist and were inspected) but do NOT currently bundle their own
    PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy, as of the exact versions pinned in
    pubspec.lock:
      * path_provider_foundation 2.6.0 — Dart-FFI-based (no compiled
        Swift/Obj-C source shipped in this version; calls Foundation
        directly via FFI bindings). No File Timestamp or other
        Required-Reason API usage was found in the available source.
      * just_audio (darwin implementation, resolved via just_audio
        0.9.46)
      * audio_service (darwin implementation, resolved via
        audio_service 0.18.19)
      * sqlite3_flutter_libs (darwin implementation, resolved via
        sqlite3_flutter_libs 0.5.42)
      * flutter_cache_manager 3.4.1 and audio_session 0.1.25
        (transitive; darwin-relevant but no bundled manifest found)

    Absence of a bundled manifest is not proof of absence of
    Required-Reason API usage — it may mean the plugin's current
    version doesn't trigger Apple's declared categories, or that its
    manifest coverage is simply incomplete for this version. This
    repository has no Xcode/macOS toolchain available to compile these
    plugins and run Apple's own manifest-merge/analysis step, so this
    was not resolved further. A future session with Xcode access must
    run an actual archive build and address any Required-Reason API
    warning Xcode surfaces before submission.
  - This app's own native code (ios/Runner/AppDelegate.swift,
    ios/Runner/SceneDelegate.swift) was read in full and contains only
    standard Flutter engine bootstrap code — no custom Required-Reason
    API usage of any kind.

  Do not add a Required-Reason API entry to this file without a matching
  source citation, exactly as this comment records for the entries
  above (all currently empty, none invented).

  This file is NOT yet added as a build resource in
  ios/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj — that file is out of this
  session's scope to modify. Adding this file to the Runner target's
  "Copy Bundle Resources" build phase in Xcode remains a required,
  separate manual step before it takes effect in an actual build.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
